= IKEA effect (technical) =

== Measurement ==
The experimental construct is commonly operationalized as a difference in self-reported valuation or willingness to pay between self-created and otherwise comparable externally created artifacts. Internal validity depends on controlling for object quality, successful task completion, time, ownership, expectations and participants' knowledge of authorship.

A causal contrast requires comparability: a higher valuation of a better customized product does not isolate a self-creation effect.

